From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:16:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 220/225] i2c: sprd-hw: switch to v1 register layout for
 sharkl5pro

The AON hw-i2c controller at 0x32060000 on sharkl5pro is the v1
"hardware channel" IP (ARM channel regs at 0x134+), not the qogirl6
v2 layout (ARM regs at 0x34+) this driver was ported from. Proven on
device: I2C_CTL bit21 (v2 TRAN_EN) does not exist/stick, and the v2
driver's ARM commands landed in the v1 HW_CHNL_PRIL/PRIH priority
registers, so every transfer faked success (0x00/rc=0 at any address,
including empty ones). Stock sharkl5Pro configs build I2C_SPRD_HW
(v1) and leave I2C_SPRD_HW_V2 off.

Replace the register map and transfer/enable/probe flow with the
vendor i2c-sprd-hw.c logic (correct 0x134+ ARM regs, addr<<10|reg<<2
command encoding, HW_CTL=0x30, NACK/bus-error reporting via
I2C_STATUS RX_ACK and CHNL_PENDING), rename the file and Kconfig
symbol to I2C_SPRD_HW, and drop the nonexistent clk_hw_i2c lookup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
